        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: હદ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હદ — had — \"a limit\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "જો તમે હદ ઓળંગશો તો હું ગુરુને ફરિયાદ કરીશ. jo tame had oḷangśo to hũ gurune phariyād karīś. If you cross the line, I will complain to the teacher."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હદ (had) is usually traced to Arabic ḥadd, \"a boundary, a limit\", through Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
